# Titan Orbit — ship simulation architecture

Fast-paced multiplayer shooter with many entities. This document is the **source of truth** for how ship movement, collision, prediction, and presentation must work. The human author does manual edits — keep code **well commented** so each file is understandable on its own.

---

## North star (read this first)

```
Player input
  → ShipInputApplySystem (client, GhostInputSystemGroup)
  → ShipMovementLogic.StepShip()  [Burst target; shared client + server]
       writes PhysicsVelocity.Linear + LocalTransform.Rotation only
  → PhysicsSystemGroup (Unity Physics integrates position, resolves collisions)
  → LocalTransform (authoritative / predicted sim state)
  → NetCode presentation + ghost interpolation
  → GameObject visual proxies (render only — never drive sim)
```

| Role | Who runs motor | Who integrates position | Who you see on screen |
|------|----------------|-------------------------|------------------------|
| Local owner | Client (predicted) | Client Unity Physics | Presentation transform |
| Remote players | Server (authority) | Server Unity Physics | NetCode ghost interpolation |
| Server sim | Server | Server Unity Physics | N/A (or host view) |

**Key idea:** Motor steers and sets velocity. **Unity Physics moves the hull and bounces off ships, planets, asteroids.** NetCode handles prediction and remote interpolation. Do not add a parallel “smoothed” movement path in MonoBehaviour.

---

## 1. NetCode owner prediction (required)

### Systems (do not merge or delete)

| System | File | World filter | Purpose |
|--------|------|--------------|---------|
| `ShipClientPredictedMovementSystem` | `ECS/Systems/ShipClientPredictedMovementSystem.cs` | `ClientSimulation` | Owner ship runs predicted motor before physics |
| `ShipMovementSystem` | `ECS/Systems/ShipMovementSystem.cs` | `ServerSimulation` | Authoritative motor for all ships |
| `ShipMovementLogic` | `ECS/Systems/ShipMovementLogic.cs` | Both call this | **Single** deterministic motor implementation |
| `ShipInputApplySystem` | `ECS/Systems/ShipInputApplySystem.cs` | Client, `GhostInputSystemGroup` | Copies pending input onto local ghost |

### Invariants

- Both movement systems live in `PredictedFixedStepSimulationSystemGroup`.
- Both run `[UpdateBefore(typeof(PhysicsSystemGroup))]` so motor sets velocity **before** physics integrates.
- Both query `.WithAll<ShipTag, Simulate>()` — `Simulate` is NetCode’s tag for entities in the prediction loop.
- Both call `ShipMovementLogic.StepShip(...)` with the same signature. **Never fork motor logic** into client-only or server-only copies.
- `TitanOrbitPhysicsBootstrapSystem` must keep `LagCompensationConfig` on client and server so predicted physics can rewind.

### Forbidden (unless user explicitly requests)

- Removing `ShipClientPredictedMovementSystem` or making owner movement server-wait / interpolation-only.
- Merging client and server into one system with conditional world checks.
- Driving owner position from `LateUpdate`, `GameObject.transform`, or non-presentation ECS reads.
- Removing `Simulate` from the movement query.

